-- title:
--   Multiples of a point of odd prime order form an odd Vélu set
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $F$, with $Q$ a point of the associated affine curve $W^{\mathrm{aff}}$. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and suppose the additive order of $Q$ is exactly $p$. Let $n$ be a natural number with $n \le (p-1)/2$ (natural subtraction and division). Then the finite set $\{\,\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(k \bullet Q) : 1 \le k \le n\,\} \subseteq F \times F$, the image of the interval $\{1,\dots,n\}$ under $k \mapsto \mathrm{coordsOrZero}(k \bullet Q)$, where $\mathrm{coordsOrZero}$ sends the point at infinity to $(0,0)$ and an affine point with coordinates $(x,y)$ to $(x,y)$, satisfies `W.IsOddVeluSet`, i.e. all three of: every pair $P$ in the set satisfies the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$ in the coordinates $(P_1,P_2)$; for every such $P$ one has $\mathrm{veluGy}(P_1,P_2) = -(2P_2 + a_1 P_1 + a_3) \neq 0$; and the first-coordinate projection is injective on the set, i.e. $P_1 = P'_1$ forces $P = P'$ for $P, P'$ in the set.
--
--   This supplies the combinatorial input to Vélu's construction of the quotient isogeny with kernel the cyclic group generated by a point of odd prime order: the chosen half-system of nonzero multiples consists of affine points, none of them $2$-torsion, with pairwise distinct abscissae. It is used in the construction of the Vélu quotient curve and map for an arbitrary odd-prime-order point, namely by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_rational_separable_isogeny_of_map_mem_zmultiples`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_rational_separable_isogeny_of_map_mem_zmultiples), [`WeierstrassCurve.stepCurve_stepSubgroup_eq_of_prime_ne_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.stepCurve_stepSubgroup_eq_of_prime_ne_two) and [`WeierstrassCurve.veluPointHom_surjective_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.veluPointHom_surjective_of_isAlgClosed).
-- source:
